Definition:
    -Builder pattern is a pattern where we can use the same construction structure to
     represent different variations of the object



How is it done:
    -Done using a private constructor so that the client is forced to use the static inner class
     and then the object is returned for method chaining.


Why Builder-Pattern:
    -If an object has a lot of fields to be initialised, then using a constructor becomes hectic and difficult
     as we have to enter a lot of constructor params and in the correct order and if some fields need not be set then we
     have to pass null.